---
description: Ask before changing an existing test when behavior changes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tests stay unless the user says to change them

When a requested functionality change would require editing an existing test, stop and ask before changing that test. Do this in Agent mode as well.

Ask in one short question: name the test and what it currently expects, then ask whether to update the test to the new behavior or keep the test and adjust the change.

Write new tests for new behavior without asking. Fix a test only when the user says it is wrong or tells you to update it.
